.TH STRUT 1
.SH NAME
strut \- ship and thruster editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/strut
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Strut
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Apps/Strut
ship editor.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Build a ship out of masses joined by springs, connectors and
thrusters, then press space to fly it against an 8192-star field.
An instruction screen is shown at startup and dismissed by any key.
.PP
The mode is held in two on-screen buttons, which may be clicked as
well as typed: the main
.BR Edit / Play
button centred at the top, and, while editing, the
.BR Mass / Spring / Connector / Thruster / Move
column down the left.
Each thruster and connector is assigned an
.I action key
when it is placed; in play, that digit fires the thruster or breaks
the connector.
.PP
.B z
and
.B Z
zoom in and out about the cursor, over the original's twenty
animation steps, so the point under the pointer stays under it.
.B d
damps the ship while it is held down, and while editing it also
unpauses the simulation so the ship settles.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "m / s / n / t / v"
.TP
.B "any key"
Dismiss the instruction screen
.TP
.B "m / s / n / t / v"
Edit modes: mass / spring / connector / thruster / move
.TP
.B 0-9
While editing, set the action key for the next thruster or connector;
in play, fire that thruster or break that connector
.TP
.B LMB
Place or edit per mode; press a mode button
.TP
.B RMB
Cycle edit mode
.TP
.B space
Toggle play and edit
.TP
.B Enter
Restart, while editing
.TP
.B c
Centre masses
.TP
.B d
Damp while held
.TP
.B z / Z
Zoom in / out about the cursor
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/strut_1.bit
Mass and thruster-nozzle sprites, one
.IB name .bit
and
.IB name .mask
each, from the
.B $SP
bins of the original.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/strut.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR ode (2),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original's File, Edit, Play and View pulldown menus are not drawn;
every entry is on a key or a mode button, and Shift-Esc (Abort) is not
distinguishable from Esc here.
The simulation integrates at h=5e-4 rather than the original's 1e-4,
because RK4 at 1e-4 does not fit the frame budget on this
implementation; app forces are computed once per tick rather than per
derivative evaluation.
.BR Noise (250,18,46)
is one random tone in that range, not white noise.
